L000534		\section{L-entropy in CFT}\label{L_cft}
L000535	Consider a 2D CFT on a circle of circumference $L$, partitioned into three contiguous arcs $A$, $B$, and $C$ arranged sequentially.
L000536	Let $l_A$ and $l_B$ denote the lengths of $A$ and $B$, respectively.
L000537	The bipartite L-entropy for the adjacent pair $(A,B)$ is
L000538	\begin{align}
L000539		\ell_{AB}^{(\mathrm{circle})}
L000540		=\frac{c}{3}\min\!\bigg\{
L000541		\log\!\Big[\frac{L}{\pi\epsilon}\frac{\sin\!\big(\pi\frac{l_A+l_B}{L}\big)\,\sin\!\big(\pi\frac{l_A}{L}\big)\,}
L000542		{\sin\!\big(\pi\frac{l_B}{L}\big)\,}\Big],\,
L000543		\log\!\Big[\frac{L}{\pi\epsilon}\frac{\sin\!\big(\pi\frac{l_A+l_B}{L}\big)\,\sin\!\big(\pi\frac{l_B}{L}\big)\,}
L000544		{\sin\!\big(\pi\frac{l_A}{L}\big)\,}\Big]
L000545		\bigg\}
L000546		+ \mathrm{const}.
L000547		\label{eq:Lcircle-min}
L000548	\end{align}
L000549	Here $\epsilon$ is the UV cutoff and the additive constant is non–universal. The overall prefactor $c/3$ encodes the universal logarithmic scaling governed by the central charge, as in single-interval entanglement entropy.
L000550	
L000551	Furthermore, we consider the whole CFT difined on an infinite line by taking the limit $L\to\infty$ which yields $\sin\left(\frac{\pi x}{L}\right)\to\frac{\pi x}{L}$. In this limit the bipartite L-entropy can be computed as
L000552	\begin{align}\label{eq:Lline-min}
L000553		\ell_{AB}^{(\mathbb{R})}
L000554		=\frac{c}{3}\min\!\bigg\{
L000555		\log\!\Big[\frac{(l_A+l_B)\,l_A}{l_B\,\epsilon}\Big],\,
L000556		\log\!\Big[\frac{(l_A+l_B)\,l_B}{l_A\,\epsilon}\Big]
L000557		\bigg\}
L000558		+ \mathrm{const}'
L000559	\end{align}
L000560	 and defining  $l_{min}\!=\!\min(l_A,l_B)$ and $l_{max}\!=\!\max(l_A,l_B)$ in compact form,
L000561	\begin{align}
L000562		\ell_{AB}^{(\mathbb{R})}
L000563		=\frac{c}{3}\,\log\!\Big[\frac{(l_A+l_B)\,l_{min}}{l_{max}\,\epsilon}\Big]
L000564		+ \mathrm{const}'.
L000565		\label{eq:Lline-compact}
L000566	\end{align}
L000567	The constants in \eqref{eq:Lcircle-min} and \eqref{eq:Lline-compact} differ by scheme-dependent terms  and are non–universal, whereas the length dependence and the coefficient $c/3$ are universal for adjacent intervals.  Note that, in both these cases, the multipartite L-entropy will be computed by considering all the other bipartite L-entropy.
